# ==============================================================================
# Panic Alarm Server — System Configuration Properties (server.env)
#
# Hospital IT Administrators can edit this file to configure network ports,
# IP bindings, and database storage paths.
#
# To apply: rename this file to "server.env" and place it next to the
# installed application executable before launching.
# ==============================================================================

# Network Port the server listens on.
# If left commented out (or set to 0), the server automatically picks the next
# free port on the machine and displays it on the login screen at startup.
# Only set this if you need a fixed port (e.g. for firewall rules).
# PORT=<port-number>

# Host network interface to bind to.
# - Use 0.0.0.0 to allow client apps on other network computers to connect.
# - Use 127.0.0.1 to lock all incoming traffic to localhost only.
# Defaults to 0.0.0.0 if not set.
# HOST=<ip-or-0.0.0.0>

# Path to the SQLite database file.
# If left commented out, the server stores the database in the secure
# OS-specific AppData directory so updates never overwrite your data.
# DB_PATH=<absolute-or-relative-path-to-database-file>
